% Praterlichter: orchestral score
% The piano waltz praterlichter.ly, orchestrated for a Johann Strauss II
% concert orchestra. GENERATED by scripts/praterlichter/compose.py from
% scripts/praterlichter/music.py; edit those and regenerate.
%
% ORCHESTRA
% Flauto piccolo, 2 flauti, 2 oboi, 2 clarinetti in B flat, 2 fagotti;
% 4 corni in F, 2 trombe in B flat, 3 tromboni; timpani (A, D / F, B flat);
% triangolo, tamburo piccolo, gran cassa e piatti; arpa; archi.
%
% LAYOUT OF THE WALTZ CHAIN (bars as printed)
% 1-21    Introduction. The head of Walzer 1 in the cellos (tenor register)
%         over harp arpeggios, pizzicato basses and a high string pad; the
%         violins and flute take it over at the B flat turn; tremolo build
%         over a timpani roll on A to a tutti fermata; flute and violins fall
%         away, solo clarinet with the violins on the last notes.
% 22-40   Walzer 1 A. First violins; afterbeats in second violins and violas;
%         clarinet guide tones; flute, horn afterbeats and bassoon join for
%         the second phrase.
% 41-57   Walzer 1 B. Line in octaves (violins, flutes); oboe and clarinet
%         chords on the accented second beats; four horns on the afterbeats;
%         trumpets and timpani at the hemiola.
% 58-74   Walzer 2 A. Violins in sixths; pizzicato violas, cellos and basses
%         with harp afterbeats; oboe, then flute and clarinet double the
%         violins; horn pedal.
% 75-90   Walzer 2 B. Flute and first violins staccato, clarinet below;
%         pizzicato strings; triangle on the high notes; piccolo in the
%         second half; wind and horn stab on the C minor 6.
% 91-109  Walzer 3 A. Timpani roll on F into the tutti: piccolo on top,
%         flutes, oboes in two parts, clarinets and second violins in sixths
%         below; trumpets on the arrival chords; trombones on bass and
%         afterbeats; bass drum every bar, cymbals on the arrivals.
% 110-125 Walzer 3 B. Running eighths in the first violins, clarinet an
%         octave below, flute in the second half; staccato afterbeats;
%         pizzicato basses; horn pedal.
% 126-133 Coda. Solo oboe over a B flat pedal; violins and flute on A7 over
%         string tremolo and a timpani roll; rising arpeggio to the tutti
%         downbeat.
% 134-149 Walzer 1 A in octaves (violins, flutes, oboes, clarinets), f.
% 150-157 Meno mosso. Solo violin and clarinet in sixths over harp and
%         pizzicato strings; horn pedal; fermata on A7.
% 158-179 Più mosso. Walzer 1 B tutti with piccolo, trumpets on every accent,
%         trombones, bass drum and cymbals; snare and timpani roll with
%         string tremolo, fp crescendo; four closing chords fff.
%
% NOTATION
% Transposing score. All music variables are at sounding pitch; the score
% applies \transpose for piccolo, clarinets, horns, trumpets and double
% basses. Tremolo bars print as abbreviations and play as repeated notes in
% the MIDI (tags 'print / 'midi). No double angle brackets anywhere.
%
